"FLINK-30090": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-30090",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Support timespan for TimerGauges",
    "description": "Unlike MeterViews, TimerGauges currently do not support timespan settings and fix the timestamp on the ViewUpdater interval which is hardcoded to 5 seconds.\r\n\r\nThis means that all metrics that use TimerGauge like backpressure, idle, busytime etc. always show the last 5 second information.\r\n\r\nWe should support timespan simiar to meterview with the same 60sec default to make these metrics more stable and useful.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "e37f5af3631ffe9250889852e85de2ff6dcc0b78",
        "message": "[FLINK-30090] Support timespan for TimerGauges",
        "author": "gyfora",
        "date": "2022-11-18T15:26:19Z",
